            <ArticleTitle>Intrathecal diamorphine during laparotomy in a patient with advanced multiple sclerosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>640-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient with advanced multiple sclerosis was successfully managed for a sigmoid colectomy using spinal anaesthesia. Effective postoperative analgesia was achieved with intrathecal diamorphine administered through an indwelling intrathecal catheter, and wound infiltration with 0.25% bupivacaine.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
